  "lineage": "Mid-1990s UK drum-and-bass subgenre integrating Jamaican ragga MC vocal samples and dancehall rhythmic vocabulary with chopped-Amen-break percussion and sub-bass production. Congo Natty (Rebel MC) inaugurated the canonical sound; Shy FX, M-Beat, General Levy, and the broader Suburban Base label roster defined the canonical 1994-1996 ragga jungle peak.",
